<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahima Sori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ibrahima Sori Mawdo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahima Sori, called Mawdo, 'the Great', was a Fulbe military leader of Futa Jallon in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>. After the death of the scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karamokho-alfa">Karamokho Alfa</a> he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> to final victory over the Jallonke and their allies and became almamy. His Soriya family then alternated the office of almamy with the Alfaya descendants of Karamokho Alfa.</p></div>
